# CI / functional tests

Project health checks via **`uv run tests ci`** and **`uv run tests functional`**. Full contract: [docs/SMOKE_TESTS.md](https://github.com/catalpainternational/catalpa-workspace-tooling/blob/main/docs/SMOKE_TESTS.md).

## When to suggest

- Validate a stack after tooling / submodule changes → `tests ci`
- Authenticated / elearning Playwright iteration → `tests functional` / `tests functional headed`
- Primary DB migrate → `dk <env> manage migrate` (not `tests ci`)

## Setup (Django compose consumers)

1. **`[dependency-groups].smoke`** in consumer repo root `pyproject.toml`
2. Tests under **`{paths.frontend}/smoke/`**
3. One-time: `uv run playwright install chromium`
4. CI hosts can use `uv sync --only-group tooling --only-group smoke` (no app install); frontend gate prefers compose `node`

## Safe local run

```bash
uv run tests ci
uv run tests functional --no-up
uv run tests functional headed --no-up
```

`tests ci` always empty-migrates an ephemeral DB (never the primary). `tests smoke` is a deprecated alias for `tests ci`. Do not run against staging/prod without explicit confirmation.

